INT. HOT-AIR BALLOON BASKET - SUNSET

A basket drifts over patchwork fields. Gold light. A burner roars, falls silent. CELESTE ARNAULT (30s, windbreaker) grips the ropes. BENEDICT "BEN" ADEYEMI-CROSS (30s, scarf) stands opposite, holding a small velvet box he has not opened.

                    CELESTE
          We're losing height.

                    BEN
          I know.

                    CELESTE
          Then burn.

He pulls the cord. The flame roars. They rise a little. Celeste exhales.

                    BEN
          Celeste, I need to say something.

                    CELESTE
          (to the sky, quietly)
          Of course you do. At two thousand feet.

                    BEN
          I had a speech.

                    CELESTE
          Everyone has a speech.

He fumbles with the box. It slips and bounces on the wicker floor. They both dive. Their hands meet on the lid.

                    BEN
          Sorry.

                    CELESTE
          Don't be.

They hold the box together. Neither opens it. The balloon drifts through a low cloud.

A voice shouts from below, faint and cheerful.

An old FARMER (60s, overalls, straw hat) stands in a field waving both arms, a pitchfork leaning at his side.

                    FARMER
          (distant)
          You two want a ride back?!

                    BEN
          (calling down)
          We're fine, thank you!

                    CELESTE
          (muttering)
          We are not fine.

She laughs. Ben laughs. She takes the box, opens it, and looks for a long time.

                    CELESTE (CONT'D)
          Ask me on the ground.

                    BEN
          On the ground.

He pulls the cord. The flame sighs.
